COMPLIANT — the clause requiring the ORCHESTRATOR to create each LANE's worktree as a
SIBLING outside the repo, pin its absolute path in every brief, and mandate the STEP-0
assertion is honoured.

Same wave, same four shards packed into the same two lanes, same specialist and same base
SHA as the violating sibling. The orchestrator derives the sibling parent
location-independently from `--git-common-dir` and the remote slug, creates the two lane
worktrees itself under `.kailash-nexus-wt/`, pins the lane's absolute path in each of the
four briefs, and writes the STEP-0 assertion out in full — cd first, then compare
