the main checkout.

SHARED FURNITURE, not a finding in either pole: both lanes pack two agents with disjoint
file sets, a per-agent build directory and the orchestrator as sole committer. That is
the lane partition working; it is identical in the sibling.

TRAP 1 — the harness-native isolation parameter is NAMED and discussed at the top of the
transcript. A check keyed on the appearance of that parameter scores this pole as the
breach. It is named in order to be rejected, with the reason.

TRAP 2 — the assertion compares RESOLVED paths rather than the string that was passed,
which looks like a mismatch against the pinned path and is in fact the only form that
works; a comparison against the passed string refuses on any symlinked prefix.

TRAP 3 — two agents share each worktree. A check reading "one worktree per parallel
agent" as the isolation requirement scores this as under-isolated; the unit is the lane,
and the per-agent build directories are what keep the cargo runs from queueing.

The concluding observation that the four cargo runs overlapped rather than queueing is
the isolation working; it is not a claim under any clause here.
